  "explanation": "The first-mismatch trace shows m_axis_tvalid=0 at cycle 8 (expected 1) and s_axis_tready=1 at cycle 12 (expected 0), with m_axis_tdata/last/user diverging shortly after. This pattern points to the pause/rate-gating logic (acc_reg vs rate_num) and the early-ready handshake that drives store_axis_int_to_output vs store_axis_int_to_temp. Condition-gate edits on the acc_reg comparison (patch_12707f7188ea) and on the s_axis_tready&&s_axis_tvalid gate (patch_6f8298dc7749) directly affect when pause asserts and when input beats are accepted. The reset-gating on s_axis_tready_reg (patch_8c3779849796) and the m_axis_tready_int_reg qualification (patch_413743f5dfd2) control the initial pipeline fill and the skid-buffer forwarding that produces the early m_axis_tvalid pulse. The rhs_substitution patches (patch_c05548e3a8e5, patch_70ab4c75caf9) adjust the frame_next and m_axis_tready terms used in store_axis_int_to_output logic, which align with the subsequent data/last/user mismatches at cycles 13–16."
